        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "noah's ark / the burning bush / allegorical image of the virgin mary as the enclosed garden and paradise of all delights",
          "formatting": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "start": 0,
              "end": 120
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "full-page miniatures from a manuscript originally created in east anglia, c. 1190-1200, containing a picture cycle of the life of christ. the book was transformed in northern england, c. 1480-90, when a second cycle of images and texts (rosary prayers and others) was integrated into the earlier cycle. the miniatures above make part of these late medieval additions. "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "source: Los Angeles, J. Paul Getty Museum, Ms. 101, ff. 10r, 13r, 79r",
